The test code basically performs a precondition to assume that the test should always pass. The actions in the contract methods are performed and their results are observed or asserted for validation.

These contracts ensure that the tested ArrayList class's behavior is consistent across different method executions. For example, when adding an element, the count should increase by one, and the index of the last occurrence of the element should increase. Similarly, when removing an element, the count should decrease by one and the index of the last occurrence of the element should decrease. This type of testing ensures that the ArrayList class correctly maintains and updates its internal structure as elements are added and removed.
